# =============================================================================
# Google Calendar + Google Tasks (Settings / Calendar / Tasks → Connect)
# =============================================================================
# Exact Cloud Console setup (do this once):
#
# 1) Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ and pick (or create) a project
# 2) APIs & Services → Library → enable BOTH:
#      • Google Calendar API
#      • Google Tasks API
# 3) APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#      • User type: External (or Internal if Workspace)
#      • Add your Google account as a Test user while in Testing
#      • Scopes used by Summit:
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendarlist.readonly
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks
# 4) APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#      • Application type: Web application
#      • Authorized JavaScript origins:
#          http://localhost:3000
#          http://127.0.0.1:3000
#      • (Optional server code flow) Authorized redirect URIs:
#          http://localhost:3000/api/google/calendar/callback
# 5) Copy the Client ID into NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below
# 6) Restart `npm run dev`, then in Summit: Settings → Connect Google
#      (or Calendar / Tasks → Connect). Allow Calendar + Tasks.
# 7) If you connected before Tasks existed: tap Reconnect for Tasks
#
# Browser connect (GIS popup) — Client ID only (recommended for local):
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
#
# Optional server OAuth code flow (needs secret + redirect URI above):
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
#
# Tokens stay on this device in localStorage (survive browser restart).
# Access tokens expire ~1h; Summit silent-refreshes when Google still grants.

# Google Solar API — auto roof measure (Measurements → Auto-measure)
# Enable "Solar API" in Cloud Console, then:
# GOOGLE_SOLAR_API_KEY=your-solar-api-key
# (or reuse GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY if Solar is enabled on that key)

# Supabase (Project Settings → API)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
